    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n39494" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">pūlĭcārĭus</span></b> , a,
			um, and <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">pūlĭcāris</span></b> , e,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>adjj.</i>
			[pulex], <i>of</i> or <i>belonging to
				fleas</i>, <i>producing fleas</i>, <i>flea-bearing</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">herba,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cael.
						Aur. Acut. 2, 37, 197</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">3, 8,
			97</span></i>.—Hence, <i>subst.</i>: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">pūlĭcārĭa</span></b> ,
				ae, f., <i>a plant</i>,
				<i>called also</i> psyllion, <i><span class="en">Theod.
					Prisc. p. 1, 10</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
